    description: "Copper Jade builds complex, gloss surfaces through movement and color variation, fired to brown-greens and creamy tan hues that break dark and pool into red tones where thick. At cone 10 it reads red/brown with some black/copper mottling. One coat gives dark greenish tones, thicker coats add greens, and the thickest applications turn to metallic red where the glaze pools. A 4 oz sample lets you test its movement and pooling reds before committing to a full pint.",
